  <title id="ctvalhohfeld-title">Hohfeld's eight jural positions</title>
  <desc id="ctvalhohfeld-desc">Two squares. Vertical lines join correlatives, one relation seen from each party: a claim-right of A against B goes with a duty of B to A, a privilege of A with a no-right of B, a power of A with a liability of B, an immunity of A with a disability of B. Dashed diagonals join opposites, two positions of the same party that exclude each other: claim-right and no-right, privilege and duty, power and disability, immunity and liability.</desc>
